/P 78 0 R
/T (Discussion: the model-size trade-off. )
/E (Discussion: the model-size trade-off. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (Qwen3.5 is larger \(6.55 GB\) and uses more memory \(5.61 GB\), but it generates 38.03 tokens/s. Gemma3 is smaller \(3.35 GB\), uses 2.91 GB of memory, and generates 20.63 tokens/s. Gemma3 loads more slowly \(19.08 s vs 0.01 s\), but its response time is shorter \(58.82 s vs 141.86 s\).)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (Therefore, Qwen3.5 is faster at generating tokens, while Gemma3 uses less memory and responds sooner in this test. The best model depends on the task, available hardware, and answer quality.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
