229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (Q15. What security risks exist when exposing a local LLM server to a network?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (Ollama has no authentication by default, so unauthorized users may access the server if it is exposed. They could consume computer resources, access prompts or sensitive data, or misuse the service. Malicious documents may also contain prompt injections that manipulate the model. A firewall can restrict access , while a reverse proxy with authentication and TLS can help protect the server and encrypt communication )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
